# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Camzify website — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the value. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# If you add a `process.env.X` anywhere, add it here too — this file is the only
# inventory of what the app needs.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Lead email (ZeptoMail) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every form submission is emailed to the team. Until the database below is
# connected, this email IS the record of the lead, so the four /api/* endpoints
# fail their request when it cannot be sent.
#
# ZEPTOMAIL_TOKEN: the "Send Mail Token" of a Mail Agent in the ZeptoMail console.
# ZEPTOMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS: an address on a domain verified in that ZeptoMail account.
# LEADS_TO_EMAIL: where the leads land. Defaults to the public contact address.
# ZEPTOMAIL_API_URL: only for the EU or India data centres
#   (https://api.zeptomail.eu/v1.1/email, https://api.zeptomail.in/v1.1/email).
ZEPTOMAIL_TOKEN=""
ZEPTOMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS="noreply@camzify.com"
ZEPTOMAIL_FROM_NAME="Camzify website"
LEADS_TO_EMAIL="contact@camzify.com"
# LEADS_CC_EMAIL: optional, comma-separated addresses copied on every lead email.
LEADS_CC_EMAIL=""
# ZEPTOMAIL_API_URL="https://api.zeptomail.com/v1.1/email"

# ── Database (optional until connected) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL connection string. Backs the four lead-capture tables in
# prisma/schema.prisma (demo requests, contact, free trial, newsletter).
#
# NOT needed to run or build the site. When set, the build applies the migrations
# in prisma/migrations (creating the four lead tables) and the four /api/* endpoints
# also write each lead there after emailing it; when unset they only email.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE?schema=public"

# ── Analytics (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_ because they're read in the browser. Neither is required
# to run or build the site — components/system/analytics-consent.tsx skips
# whichever script has no ID set, and skips both entirely if neither is set.
#
# Vercel Web Analytics and Speed Insights (app/layout.tsx) need no ID and no
# consent gate: both are cookieless, so they always run.
#
# These two DO set cookies and load only after a visitor accepts the cookie
# banner (app/cookie-policy describes exactly what each one sets):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID: the GA4 Measurement ID, from
#   Google Analytics → Admin → Data Streams → your web stream (format G-XXXXXXXXXX).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID: the Project ID from
#   Microsoft Clarity → Settings → Setup → the ID in the tracking snippet.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=""
